{title: It Is Well with My Soul}
{artist: Horatio Spafford / Philip Bliss}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: C}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 413장}
{title_ko: 내 평생에 가는 길}
{score: it-is-well.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]When peace like a [F]river at[C]tendeth my way
When [C]sorrows like [G]sea billows [C]roll
Whatever my [F]lot, Thou hast [C]taught me to say
[C]It is well, [F]it is well with my [C]soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]It is well [F]with my [C]soul
[G]It is well, it is well with my [C]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Though Satan should [F]buffet, though [C]trials should come
Let this [C]blest assurance [G]con[C]trol
That Christ hath re[F]garded my [C]helpless estate
And hath [C]shed His own [F]blood for my [C]soul
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]My sin, oh the [F]bliss of this [C]glorious thought
My sin, not in [G]part but the [C]whole
Is nailed to the [F]cross and I [C]bear it no more
Praise the [C]Lord, praise the [F]Lord, O my [C]soul
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]And Lord haste the [F]day when my [C]faith shall be sight
The clouds be [C]rolled back as a [G]scroll
The trump shall re[F]sound and the [C]Lord shall descend
Even [C]so, it is [F]well with my [C]soul
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
